  faqs: [
    { question: "Where do I even start looking for an IB tutor if I live in Durg?", answer: "Send us the programme, subject, level and exam session your child is on, and we put forward tutors already experienced in that exact combination. Since no school inside Durg teaches the IB in any form, the shortlist is built entirely on syllabus fit rather than location. A free trial lesson always comes first, and a wrong fit simply means we look again." },
    { question: "Can you match an IGCSE tutor who actually knows the Cambridge syllabus for a Durg student?", answer: "Yes. Cambridge is the board behind Rungta Public School in Bhilai, the nearest confirmed IGCSE option to Durg, and tutors get matched by the exact code and tier a student studies, Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620 among the common ones, working from Cambridge's own past papers and mark schemes throughout." },
    { question: "Will a tutor actually come to our house in Durg?", answer: "No. That kind of in-person arrangement exists only in Gurugram and a handful of Delhi NCR neighbourhoods. Everywhere else, Durg included, what we run is a live, one-to-one video lesson with a shared whiteboard standing in for a tutor at the table. It is genuine online tuition delivered into your home, just not a doorstep visit." },
    { question: "How much does an IB or IGCSE tutor for a Durg student typically cost?", answer: "It depends on the programme and level, the subject itself, how long each session runs, and how recently the tutor has taught that exact syllabus, and we confirm the number for your specific match before the trial starts. Diploma HL subjects generally cost more than IGCSE Core work. Every session runs online, so travel never enters the fee, and nothing locks you into a long contract." },
    { question: "Is there any school actually inside Durg that teaches IB or IGCSE?", answer: "No, not within the city's own boundary. Rungta Public School in Bhilai, about twenty kilometres away, teaches Cambridge IGCSE alongside CBSE, and Rungta International School in Raipur, roughly forty kilometres off, is Chhattisgarh's sole IB World School; N.H. Goel World School nearby adds a further Cambridge option. Durg's own schools run on the Chhattisgarh Board, CBSE, or, for one school, ICSE." },
    { question: "My son boards at an IB school away from Durg. Can tutoring fit around his holidays?", answer: "Yes, and it is one of the more frequent requests we get from this district, since no local or nearby school teaches the Diploma or Middle Years Programme inside Durg itself. A tutor gets matched to the precise subject, level and syllabus his boarding school follows, with sessions built around school breaks or, where the school allows it, agreed slots during term." },
    { question: "Do I have to commit to anything before trying this out?", answer: "No. Every match opens with a free trial lesson, where your child works through a genuine topic from their own syllabus at no cost and with nothing owed afterward. The tutor then sends a short plan for the first month, and it is entirely your decision whether to continue, ask for changes, or try someone else." },
    { question: "Can a tutor write or fix my daughter's IB Internal Assessment?", answer: "No, though they can guide the process closely: helping settle on a workable research question, unpacking what each assessment criterion actually rewards, planning data collection, and giving honest feedback on drafts. Producing or rewriting the assessed work itself breaches IB's own integrity rules, so our tutors decline that request every time." },
    { question: "What IB Diploma subjects can a Durg family actually get help with?", answer: "Coverage runs across the major Diploma subject groups a boarding student from Durg is likely to be taking: both Maths routes at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, along with Theory of Knowledge and the Extended Essay." },
    { question: "Do you help with MYP or PYP work too, or only the Diploma, for children connected to Durg?", answer: "The full continuum is covered. MYP support usually centres on criterion-based analysis across the sciences and language subjects, plus the Personal Project's process journal, while PYP work builds reading, writing, number sense and the research skills the Exhibition needs." },
    { question: "Is an online tutor really as good as sitting in a classroom for these boards?", answer: "For a district with no IB or Cambridge school at all, it holds up very well in practice. A shared whiteboard, live screen-shared past papers and recorded worked examples cover nearly everything a tutor at your child's side would otherwise offer, while opening the choice of tutor to specialists anywhere in India rather than just those near Bhilai or Raipur." },
    { question: "How do you actually check that a tutor knows what they're teaching?", answer: "Every tutor's qualifications, recent teaching history in that specific subject and level, and approach to Internal Assessment guidance get reviewed before a name reaches any family. Given that Durg itself has no IB or Cambridge school, we deliberately look for people who have taught the exact syllabus recently rather than generalists. The free trial lesson is then where you form your own judgement." },
    { question: "At what point should my child in Durg actually begin tutoring?", answer: "Right at the start of the course works best, Class 11 for the Diploma or Grade 9 for Cambridge IGCSE, since that leaves time to fix foundations before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades land. Starting later, even in the final year, can still move the needle, with the plan narrowed to whichever topics and past papers carry the most marks." },
    { question: "We're thinking of moving our child from CBSE to IGCSE. Is that realistic from Durg?", answer: "Very much so, and it is a request we see often, usually pointing toward Rungta Public School in Bhilai or preparation as a private candidate. The real adjustment tends to be question style rather than content, since command words like 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' need to be taught directly, ideally starting a term before the actual switch." },
    { question: "Can classes be scheduled in the evening or on weekends for a Durg household?", answer: "Yes, most families here book weekday evenings once school finishes, along with weekend mornings. Scheduling takes account of the district's summer heat, when an earlier evening slot usually suits better, and of the crowds around Durg Junction during festival season. Adding a second weekly slot ahead of an exam series is a straightforward request." },
    { question: "What if the tutor we're matched with just isn't the right fit?", answer: "Tell us, and we find someone else straight away. Progress gets reviewed with every family every few weeks, and a re-match happens whenever the fit is wrong, rather than expecting a child to push through with someone who isn't working. There is no long contract, so pausing or stopping carries no penalty either." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram have any tie-up with schools in Durg, Bhilai or Raipur, or with the IB itself?", answer: "None at all. IB Gram operates as an independent tutoring platform with no affiliation to, endorsement from, or representation of St Xavier's High School, Rungta Public School, Rungta International School, N.H. Goel World School, the International Baccalaureate Organization or Cambridge Assessment International Education. Schools appear on this page only to show where Durg families actually study or board." },
    { question: "Does living in the Durg-Bhilai belt specifically change how tutoring gets arranged?", answer: "It shapes the context more than the lesson itself. Tutors matched here understand that there is no local IB or Cambridge school, that IGCSE means a trip to Bhilai and the Diploma means one to Raipur, and that scheduling has to account for Durg Junction's own festival-season crowds. The class itself still runs online exactly as it would anywhere else." },
  ],

